'''''Ulota crispa''''', the '''crisped pincushion moss''',{{r|ns}} is a species of acrocarpous moss in the genus ''[[Ulota]]'' native to eastern [[North America]]. It is generally found in tight mounds on tree bark.<ref>{{Cite web|title=''Ulota crispa'' in Flora of North America @ efloras.org|url=http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=1&taxon_id=200001670|access-date=2021-07-01|website=www.efloras.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=''Ulota crispa'' – Bryophytes of Hoxie Gorge|url=https://sites.cortland.edu/bryophytes/field-guide/mosses/acrocarp/ulota-crispa/|access-date=2021-07-01|language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=''Ulota crispa'' {{!}} International Plant Names Index|url=https://www.itis.gov/servlet/SingleRpt/SingleRpt?search_topic=TSN&search_value=15909#null|access-date=2021-07-01|website=www.ipni.org}}</ref>

